{{also|Locket}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|loquet}}, from a diminutive of {{der|en|xno|loc}}, itself from {{der|en|ang|loc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɑkɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-locket.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒkɪt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[pendant]] that opens to reveal a space used for storing a [[photograph]] or other small item.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} The upper metallic cap of a sword’s [[scabbard]].
# A small white [[marking]] on a cat's [[coat]].

